>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `split_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.split_ss : simpLib.ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Splits case expressions during simplification.

`split_ss` is a fragment named `"split"`. Its looper, `"splitter"`,
applies `splitLib.SPLIT_TAC` with the split rules for the datatypes whose
case constants occur fully applied in the goal, and with the rules that
have the persistent `[split]` attribute. The fragment also rewrites
`(b ==> t) /\ (~b ==> t)` to `t`.

`ExclX "split:name"` excludes a `[split]` rule from one call, and
`ExclX "case:ty"` the splitting of type `ty`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.++ (boolSimps.bool_ss,
     simpLib.split_ss);
>> simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss []
     ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) (Context.snapshot());
```

